{title: Down in the Valley}
{artist: Traditional American}
{key: G}
{tempo: 108}
{time: 3/4}
{difficulty: beginner}
{tags: folk, americana, waltz}
{comment: Just two chords: a good first song for changing between G and D7.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Down in the [G]valley, the [G]valley so [D7]low
[D7]Hang your head [D7]over, hear the [D7]wind [G]blow
[G]Hear the wind [G]blow, dear, [G]hear the wind [D7]blow
[D7]Hang your head [D7]over, hear the [D7]wind [G]blow

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Roses love [G]sunshine, [G]violets love [D7]dew
[D7]Angels in [D7]heaven know [D7]I love [G]you
[G]Know I love [G]you, dear, [G]know I love [D7]you
[D7]Angels in [D7]heaven know [D7]I love [G]you

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Write me a [G]letter, send it [G]by [D7]mail
[D7]Send it in [D7]care of the [D7]Birmingham [G]jail
[G]Birmingham [G]jail, love, [G]Birmingham [D7]jail
[D7]Send it in [D7]care of the [D7]Birmingham [G]jail
